  "title": "How to Solve Quadratic Simultaneous Equations",
  "content": "<p>When one equation is linear and one is quadratic (or circle), use <strong>substitution</strong>.</p><p>1. Rearrange the linear equation for one variable.</p><p>2. Substitute into the quadratic.</p><p>3. Solve the resulting quadratic.</p><p>4. Back-substitute to find the other variable.</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>Solve</strong> \\(y = x + 1\\) and \\(y = x^2 - 3\\)</p><p>\\(x + 1 = x^2 - 3\\) → \\(x^2 - x - 4 = 0\\)</p><p>Use the formula or factorise to find both solutions.</p>"
